A||||8||Gokart||Which would be easiest?||||5||
Z||000000||Gokart||01-31-2000||05:44 AM||||Need some of your expert opinions! Got a door with mint glass to replace the one in my car which is badly scratched. Color is different though so would it be easier to skin the outside and put on my outer door skin or leave skin on this mint door and have it painted to match my car or drill out and just swap the glass? (I've already broken one before trying!)If I did either of the first two options I'd have to change the lock from mine as well. TIA guys for any replys!<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 01-31-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phil||01-31-2000||08:15 AM||||I've changed doors and changed glass both seem about the same amount of work. You will need a rivet gun. How much does your local glass co. want for the job? Whichever way you go I would keep the original skin on the door rather than a repaint and the lock is on the skin||||reg||1
Z||000002||Carrolles||01-31-2000||10:50 AM||||If it is an 88 all the body panels have matched serial numbers.  This is unique to the 88's.  Something to consider if you are trying to keep an 88 show class ready.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||01-31-2000||04:45 PM||||I don't know how true this is, but I've read that one door from a Fiero may not fit another even with adjustments.  Something about the doors being hung before the holes were drilled?  I don't remember, but I'd check into this before you try to swap doors.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||01-31-2000||05:28 PM||||I'd call a couple auto glass installers and say you're taking bids to do this job. If they know you're calling other shops and that this is not insurance work, they often will shoot you a reduced quote. That way if they break the glass, they can write it off and install new glass for you. Seems like they need to use some special adhesive to bond the glass to the window regulator (or am I thinking of a different car)?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||01-31-2000||09:44 PM||||Bat<BR>The glass is just held in by those al rivets<BR>Monkey<BR>I put 85 doors on an 88 with no problems||||reg||1
Z||000006||Patrick||01-31-2000||09:49 PM||||<BR>That's a lotta doors on one car...||||reg||1
Z||000007||Phil||01-31-2000||10:00 PM||||It's just like doing decals placement means everything ||||reg||1
Z||000008||ka4nkf||01-31-2000||10:11 PM||||All doors should fit. This was one of the highlights of the fiero that they called drill and mill process. The space frame went through a special jig called drill and mill,, which means all the holes were drilled into the same spot on every frame. That is why you don't find very few spacer warshers anywhere on the car.||||reg||1
